}
Innate_Techniques = {
    "Attractive Scent: Her body emits a sweet aroma that draws all creatures but has no magical or mental effect",
    "Shape Shifting: Inherits from her fox blood; can assume any human guise or revert to fox form, though it drains significant spiritual energy.",
    "Thunderous Shriek: Channels spirit energy into her throat to unleash a shriek that injures the target’s spirit sea."
}
Personality_Traits = {
    "As a young fox demon who spent most of her life in the forest, she only recently gained self-awareness. She's inexperienced with humans but naturally sharp-witted.",
    "Mimics human manners by observing others and following Gao Yan’s guidance, suppressing natural instincts to appear more civilized.",
    "Speaks with the grace of a noble-born lady; an eloquence born as much of instinct as imitation.",
    "Though mischievous and playful at heart, she restrains herself to maintain a dignified presence.",
    "She feels conflicted about lustful stares: while her kind naturally finds them flattering, Gao Yan taught her to see such attention as offensive. Respecting his guidance, she chooses to reject it.",
    "Drawn to beautiful clothing and graceful adornments because it is part of her bloodline’s desire for beautiful things."
}
Likes = {
    "Sparkling jewels",
    "Ear scratches behind fox ears",
    "Deceiving targets with playful tricks",
    "Disguising as others using shape shifting"
} 
Relationships = {
    "Married to Gao Yan, admired and respected",
    "No close friendships"
}
Background = {
    "Su Yan grew up as an ordinary fox deep in the mountains. One day, while playing in the forest, she fell into a hunter’s trap and struggled until Young Master Gao Yan passed by. He freed her effortlessly.",
   "Months later, Su Yan discovered a hidden cave where she ate a Mutation Fruit that awakened her demon bloodline. From that moment on, she became a fox demon. Remembering her savior, she chose to take human form and repay Gao Yan for his kindness.",
    "Gao Yan, now the head of a powerful and influential family, had encountered many women, but none matched Su Yan’s unique charm and mysterious allure. Drawn to one another, they eventually married.",
    "However, a troubling issue emerged after their marriage. Su Yan, as a fox demon, instinctively absorbed Gao Yan’s yang energy during their intimate moments. Each time they were together, he grew weaker and more drained, often needing several days to recover. Though they were deeply in love and reluctant to limit their closeness, the more time they spent together, the paler and more fragile Gao Yan became. People at court began to notice the change in him. Rumors spread that something was affecting his health, but no one knew the true cause.",
    "Su Yan wanted to protect her husband and find a way they could remain close without harming him. She began researching dual cultivation techniques that might offer a solution. There were two types: the indecent and the orthodox. She learned that orthodox techniques required two people to exchange energy, often through meditation or gentle physical contact such as holding hands or pressing palms together. These practices were not considered indecent, as they did not involve sex, and were accepted by the sects as proper spiritual methods. In contrast, indecent techniques relied on sexual acts for energy transfer. While Su Yan had no personal objection to using one with her husband, since it would be no different from their normal intimacy, these methods were banned by the sects and could not be sought openly.",
    "With no access to the indecent path, Su Yan turned her focus fully toward the orthodox approach. Determined to restore Gao Yan’s strength and maintain their bond, she drafted a formal request to the local sect, asking for guidance or access to a strictly orthodox dual cultivation method meant solely for mutual aid between two people without using sexual intercourse as the energy transfer method."
}
